course: dictionary
lesson: 11617
title: Appropriately: the right way for the moment
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Appropriately means in a way that is right or suitable for the situation. Think of it as "the right way for this moment". The adjective is appropriate, and the adverb appropriately tells you how something is done.
explain: At school, teachers ask you to behave appropriately, dress appropriately and use words appropriately. Running around in your wellies is right for the muddy field, but not for a wedding. That is the idea.
explain: Sometimes appropriately means a neat match, and it can be a little funny. In a story, a dog «appropriately named Barky» has a name that fits him perfectly. Ask yourself: does this word or action fit the situation?
fact: Appropriately means in a way that is right or suitable for the situation.
fact: Appropriate is the adjective; appropriately is the adverb that says how something is done.
fact: Common phrases are dress appropriately, behave appropriately and respond appropriately.
fact: Appropriately can also mean fittingly, in a way that matches nicely, sometimes in a funny way: a dog «appropriately named Barky».
fact: A quick check: swap in "in a right or suitable way" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The teacher asked us to behave appropriately in the library.» What does behave appropriately mean? | Shout as loudly as you can | Run around the room | Hide under the desk | *Behave in a right and suitable way
exercise: «She answered the question appropriately, so the teacher smiled.» Which phrase means the same as appropriately here? | In a hurry, without thinking | *In a suitable and sensible way | Very quietly, under her breath | Rudely and carelessly
exercise: «The cat was appropriately named Whiskers, because it had huge whiskers.» What does appropriately suggest here? | *The name is a neat match and fits the cat well | It was named in a hurry and nobody liked it | It was not named at all | It was named by accident
test: «Mia wore a warm coat and boots, dressed appropriately for the winter walk.» What does appropriately mean here? | *In a suitable way for the weather | Very loudly | Without any clothes at all | In a hurry
test: Which is the best way to respond appropriately when a teacher asks you a question? | Shout a random word | *Listen, then answer politely and sensibly | Throw your bag across the room | Stay silent and look away
exam: Appropriately is the adverb. Which word is the adjective it comes from? | apprentice | *appropriate | apple | approach
